{
 "pmid": "35663805",
 "instructions_version": "extract_v6",
 "reports_individuals_with_tnfaip3_variant": true,
 "relevance_note": "Single adult case report of a clinically (radiologically) diagnosed ATS patient without genetic testing: 'The diagnosis of ATS was made due to typical radiological findings. Genetic or molecular testing was not done for the patient.'",
 "method_note": "Read by hand; no script transcription. One in-scope person (diagnosis of ATS, no SLC2A10 variant reported because genetic testing was not done), so the variants table is empty. n_patients_reported left null: the paper reports no patient with a SLC2A10 variant and states no count. Age at diagnosis and at report both taken as the stated 33 years. Checklist 'stenosis of the aorta or aortic branches' left not reported because the paper says only 'no ... significant stenosis' (a qualified absence); 'aortic root aneurysm' marked excluded from 'No appreciable aneurysms' on the CT aortogram. Pulmonary artery stenosis excluded from 'no evidence of stenosis' on CT pulmonary angiogram. Inguinal hernia observed from a past repair of a right inguinal hernia. Pelvic venous congestion comes from the Fig. 1 legend. No contradictions found. Country not recorded: only the hospital (ethics approval) is named.",
